[Chapter "Against ...e6"]
[Line "The check on b4"]
[Opening "Rapport-Jobava System"]

{Black answers Nb5 with a bishop check instead of guarding c7.} 1. d4 {Start with the queen's pawn.} 1... d5 2. Nc3 {The Jobava idea: the knight comes to c3 before the c-pawn moves, ready for Nb5 or e4.} 2... Nf6 3. Bf4 {Develop the bishop outside the pawn chain before e3.} 3... e6 4. Nb5 {Hit c7.} 4... Bb4+ 5. c3 {Block the check with a pawn and gain a tempo on the bishop.} 5... Ba5 6. Nf3 {Develop. The bishop on a5 is out of play for now, and b4 may chase it further later.} *
